/* Thrones module: 05-act5-arc-sacrifice.partial.if */
scene__
  @name "ACT5: The Price of Blood"
  @first "The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast"
  @sections "The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast" "The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell" "Winterfell Night Council before witnesses" "The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners" "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery" "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light" "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals" "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries" "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke" "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog" "Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood" "The Wall War Map against old law" "Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky" "Moat Cailin Whispered Warning at the gatehouse" "Oldtown Silent Betrayal behind closed doors" "Pyke Hostage Exchange at the broken tower" "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow" "Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn" "The Trident Salt Pact by the harbor chain" "Riverrun Broken Oath under rain" "The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast" "The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell" "Winterfell Night Council before witnesses" "The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners"
__scene

section__
  @title "The Kingsroad Blackmail Ledger after the feast"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-arc-sacrifice/frame-361.jpg"

  "Along the Kingsroad, sour ale and horse sweat hang over a ledger full of purchased silence. House Valehart now sits at the hinge of three theaters, and your ruling here will redirect riders, stores, and hostages before dawn. Sansa Stark tests your posture in public while Brienne of Tarth studies your pauses for weakness, and every scribe in the room is already drafting competing versions of your intent. What began as policy at the battlefront has become names on funeral cloth.

The war has moved from strategy to accounting for the dead. Families demand justice while commanders demand silence to keep lines intact.

You can answer loss with formal justice and shared burden, or with private enforcement that keeps control while deepening resentment. Either path secures something now and burns something you cannot rebuild quickly."

  choice__
    @target "The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Read the order in open council, publish penalties, and spend reputation to stabilize lawful compliance."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Winterfell Night Council before witnesses"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Suppress the full record, pressure the weakest brokers quietly, and convert fear into immediate operational control."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "The Red Keep Raven Intercept before the sept bell"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-arc-sacrifice/frame-362.jpg"

  "Before the sept bell in the capital, raven feathers and hot wax litter the floor around forged orders. House Valehart now sits at the hinge of three theaters, and your ruling here will redirect riders, stores, and hostages before dawn. Brienne of Tarth tests your posture in public while Sansa Stark studies your pauses for weakness, and every scribe in the room is already drafting competing versions of your intent. The camps are full of kin demanding meaning for losses that cannot be reversed.

Irreversible choices are stacking. Mercy can look weak, cruelty can look necessary, and either one can poison the settlement you still hope to reach.

You can answer loss with formal justice and shared burden, or with private enforcement that keeps control while deepening resentment. Either path secures something now and burns something you cannot rebuild quickly."

  choice__
    @target "Winterfell Night Council before witnesses"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Confirm the plan by written oath, let rivals contest it publicly, and secure long-term trust over speed."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 7)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Run split instructions through deniable couriers, isolate rivals from their allies, and keep leverage off the books."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "Winterfell Night Council before witnesses"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-arc-sacrifice/frame-363.jpg"

  "In Winterfell at night, pine smoke and snowmelt drift through a council chamber packed with wary bannermen. House Valehart now sits at the hinge of three theaters, and your ruling here will redirect riders, stores, and hostages before dawn. Catelyn Stark tests your posture in public while Arya Stark studies your pauses for weakness, and every scribe in the room is already drafting competing versions of your intent.

Your officers are carrying losses they cannot replace. If you mishandle this moment, survivors obey out of fear and never trust again.

You can answer loss with formal justice and shared burden, or with private enforcement that keeps control while deepening resentment. Either path secures something now and burns something you cannot rebuild quickly."

  choice__
    @target "The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Call captains into formal hearing, fix responsibility in record, and pay the time cost to restore legitimacy."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Make examples in shadow, leak only what serves your position, and lock compliance through controlled uncertainty."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "The Twins Debt Collection under wolf banners"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/05-act5-arc-sacrifice/frame-364.jpg"

  "At the Twins, river mist and rotting rope surround toll tables where every number is a weapon. House Valehart now sits at the hinge of three theaters, and your ruling here will redirect riders, stores, and hostages before dawn. Arya Stark tests your posture in public while Catelyn Stark studies your pauses for weakness, and every scribe in the room is already drafting competing versions of your intent.

Now the cost is personal. Every new order names people, not just positions, and grief is starting to outrank discipline in camp decisions.

You can answer loss with formal justice and shared burden, or with private enforcement that keeps control while deepening resentment. Either path secures something now and burns something you cannot rebuild quickly."

  choice__
    @target "Harrenhal Torchlit Census at the rookery"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 2, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Set one public standard for all houses, enforce it by decree, and accept short-term outrage for durable cohesion."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 5)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 2, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Turn hidden debts into blackmail leverage, compel cooperation without hearings, and preserve tempo at moral cost."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
    @when ((wealth + essos_ties + dragon_factor) >= 11)
    @action wealth = clampStat(wealth - 1, 0, 30)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 1, 0, 30)
    @action dragon_factor = clampStat(dragon_factor + 1, 0, 30)
    "Spend coin on Essosi couriers and dragon-backed deterrence, buying speed while draining treasury reserves."
  __choice
